adbd: report the handheld's own product identity, not a Nexus 4

adbd's CNXN banner carries ro.product.name/model/device, and this build has the
property lookups commented out, so it falls back to the compiled defaults --
occam / Nexus 4 / mako (Android's own test device). A host then lists the
handheld as `product:occam model:Nexus_4 device:mako`. Use Banana's values.

--- a/core/adbd/adb.c
+++ b/core/adbd/adb.c
@@ -302,9 +302,9 @@
     };
     static const int num_cnxn_props = ARRAY_SIZE(cnxn_props);
     static const char *values[] = {
-        "occam",
-        "Nexus 4",
-        "mako",
+        "banana",
+        "Pocket Classic",
+        "rpc",
     };
     int i;
     size_t remaining = bufsize;
